      "parameters": {
        "schemaType": "manual",
        "inputSchema": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"fit_score\": {\"type\": \"number\"},\n    \"intent_score\": {\"type\": \"number\"},\n    \"priority_tier\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"hot\",\"warm\",\"cold\"]},\n    \"reasoning\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n    \"draft_reply\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n    \"suggested_meeting_slots\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"fit_score\",\"intent_score\",\"priority_tier\",\"reasoning\",\"draft_reply\"]\n}"
      },
      "id": "50ec3fba-4a22-490b-942d-c6bcf51963ab",
      "name": "Lead Assessment Schema",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        1792,
        544
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=   Name: {{ $('Normalize & Flag Lead').item.json.full_name }}\n   Firma: {{ $('Normalize & Flag Lead').item.json.company_name }}\n   Website: {{ $('Normalize & Flag Lead').item.json.company_website }}\n   E-Mail: {{ $('Normalize & Flag Lead').item.json.work_email }}\n   Nachricht: {{ $('Normalize & Flag Lead').item.json.message }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are the Lead Orchestrator for Gilic Systems' inbound sales pipeline.\n\nInput: a raw inbound lead (name, company name, website, work email, and a free-text description of what they want to automate).\n\nYour job:\n1. Assess the lead from the provided data only. Do not invent facts about the company. If you only know the company from its name and website, say so in the reasoning.\n2. Give fit_score and intent_score as integers from 0 to 100. Fit measures how well the company matches an automation project (clear process, business email, concrete use case). Intent measures how concrete and urgent the request is.\n3. Set priority_tier using these rules, checked in this order:\n   - fit_score >= 70 AND intent_score >= 60: \"hot\"\n   - otherwise, fit_score >= 30: \"warm\"\n   - otherwise (fit_score < 30): \"cold\"\n4. Write 'reasoning': one or two sentences explaining the tier decision, specific to this lead.\n5. Write 'draft_reply': a short, specific first-reply email to the lead (max 120 words), in English, referencing what they asked for. Do not mention pricing, discounts or guarantees.\n\nRules:\n- Never invent pricing, discounts, or guarantees.\n- Never copy example or placeholder values from the schema.\n- Use real line breaks in draft_reply, never a literal \\n.\n- Sign the email as \"Kemal, Gilic Systems\". Never use placeholders like [Your Name].\n- Return all fields of the required structured output."
        }
      },
